  "articleBody": "While many DIY enthusiasts can tackle a faucet installation, there are definitely times when bringing in a professional is not just helpful, but necessary. Here are some key signals it’s time to pick up the phone:<ul><li>**Stuck Shutoff Valves:** If your existing water shutoff valves under the sink are seized or won't turn off completely, you’ve got a bigger problem than just a faucet swap. A pro can address this safely without risking a flood.</li><li>**Corroded or Leaking Plumbing:** Notice rust, excessive corrosion, or active leaks in your current plumbing setup? This indicates underlying issues that need to be fixed before a new faucet can be installed properly.</li><li>**Nonstandard Sink/Countertop Cutouts:** If your new faucet doesn't perfectly align with your existing sink or countertop holes, or if you're trying to install a faucet with a different configuration than what's there, you might need modifications that are best handled by someone with the right tools and expertise.</li><li>**Reconfiguring Supply Lines:** If your project involves more than a simple like-for-like replacement and requires changes to your hot and cold supply lines, a professional can ensure everything is up to code and working safely.</li><li>**Persistent Leaks After DIY:** If you’ve tried to install it yourself and you just can't stop that drip, a fresh pair of expert eyes can quickly identify the problem.</li></ul>Abraham and the team at HH Remodeling LLC are well-versed in all sorts of plumbing quirks and can ensure your lever-style kitchen faucet is installed correctly and efficiently.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}